<DocsLayout title="Install — Tether CLI" description="Install Tether on macOS or Linux with the install script, Homebrew, mise, a static Linux release download, or from source.">
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">GET STARTED</p>
    <h1>Install Tether</h1>
    <p>Tether runs on macOS and on x86_64 and aarch64 Linux. Install it on each machine you want to sync.</p>

    <h2>Install script (macOS and Linux)</h2>
    <Code code="curl -fsSL https://tether-cli.com/install.sh | sh" />
    <p>The script finds the build for your system, checks its <code>.sha256</code> file and installs <code>tether</code> to <code>~/.local/bin</code>. Run it again to upgrade. If the systemd user service runs, the script restarts it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>TETHER_INSTALL_DIR</code> sets another directory</li>
      <li><code>TETHER_VERSION</code> installs one release, such as <code>2.1.0</code></li>
    </ul>
    <Code code="curl -fsSL https://tether-cli.com/install.sh | TETHER_VERSION=2.1.0 sh" />

    <h2>Homebrew (macOS and Linux)</h2>
    <Code code={`brew tap paddo-tech/tap
brew install tether-cli`} />
    <p>Homebrew on Linux uses the same commands.</p>

    <h2>Release download (Linux)</h2>
    <p>Each <a href="https://github.com/paddo-tech/tether-cli/releases">GitHub release</a> has a static Linux build for each CPU. These builds do not need a specific glibc, so they run on any distribution.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>x86_64:</strong> <code>tether-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz</code></li>
      <li><strong>aarch64:</strong> <code>tether-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz</code></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Download the tarball and its <code>.sha256</code> file. Check the checksum. Then put the <code>tether</code> binary in a directory on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
    <Code code={`target=x86_64-unknown-linux-musl   # or aarch64-unknown-linux-musl
base=https://github.com/paddo-tech/tether-cli/releases/latest/download
curl -fLO "$base/tether-$target.tar.gz"
curl -fLO "$base/tether-$target.tar.gz.sha256"
sha256sum -c "tether-$target.tar.gz.sha256"
tar -xzf "tether-$target.tar.gz"
install -D -m 755 tether ~/.local/bin/tether`} />
    <p>Each tarball holds only the <code>tether</code> binary. The <code>latest</code> URL gets the newest release.</p>

    <h2>mise</h2>
    <Code code="mise use -g github:paddo-tech/tether-cli" />
    <p>mise gets the release builds from GitHub. It lists a new release only after its version cache updates, so for a release from the last hours, name the version: <code>github:paddo-tech/tether-cli@2.1.0</code>.</p>

    <h2>From source</h2>
    <p>You need Rust 1.91 or later.</p>
    <Code code="cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/paddo-tech/tether-cli" />

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Git</strong>, with access to a private repository on GitHub, GitLab or your own server</li>
      <li><strong>curl</strong>, for the OSV malware checks</li>
      <li><strong>The package managers you sync</strong>: Homebrew, npm, pnpm, bun, gem or uv</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Next</h2>
    <p>New to Tether: follow the <a href="/docs/quick-start">Quick start</a>. Upgrading from 1.x: read <a href="/docs/upgrade">Upgrade from 1.x</a> first.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
